    deficitFriction: 'Metal governs the capacity for incision, refinement, and surgical precision. When Metal is deficient, the decision-making apparatus loses its cutting edge. You experience "perfect completion paralysis" — a recursive refinement loop that prevents closure. The professional cost is severe: delayed market entry, missed partnership windows, and a reputation for intellectual brilliance that never materializes into output. Metal deficiency does not affect the quality of your thinking — it cripples the quality of your finishing.',
